n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1+\\pi ,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1+\\pi ) & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+\\pi -1) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at the point $(1+\\pi ,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =0(x-(1+\\pi )) \\\\ y+3 & =0 \\\\ y & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["9207df1b-4a6c-533b-b78e-f5d2674e1371"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "340044b2-b48d-5eb9-817c-624479f49ac2" :answer/id #uuid "340044b2-b48d-5eb9-817c-624479f49ac2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18 \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a8942c70-e5be-58bd-9441-c89f4912e367" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8942c70-e5be-58bd-9441-c89f4912e367" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["340044b2-b48d-5eb9-817c-624479f49ac2"] :answer-field/correct "340044b2-b48d-5eb9-817c-624479f49ac2" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "efb4aba1-7652-55ac-8883-4dc872ffd09b" :question/id #uuid "efb4aba1-7652-55ac-8883-4dc872ffd09b" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of $y =\\sin \\left(\\pi \\left(8x^{2} + 2x - 2\\right)\\right)$ at $x = 1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y = f(x)$ at $x=1$ is given by $f'(1).$\n\nWe will calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n\\[\ny = \\sin{u}, \\qquad u = \\pi \\left(8x^{2} +2x - 2\\right).\n\\]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = \\cos{u}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\pi (16x + 2).\n\\]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n\\begin{align*}\nf'(x) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\cos u \\cdot \\pi (16x+2)\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\pi (16x+2)\\cos u\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\pi (16x+2)\\cos \\left(  \\pi \\left(8x^{2} +2x - 2\\right) \\right).\n\\end{align*}\n\nEvaluating at $x=1,$ we find\n\n\\begin{align}\nf'(1) & =\\pi (16\\cdot1+2)\\cos \\left(  \\pi \\left(8\\cdot1^{2} +2\\cdot1 - 2\\right) \\right) \\\\[3pt]\n\n& =18\\pi \\cos(8\\pi) \\\\[3pt]\n&= 18\\pi \\cdot (1) \\\\[3pt]\n&= 18 \\pi\n\\end{align}\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of $y = f(x)$ at $x = 1$ is \n\\[\nm = f'(1) = \\bbox[4pt, border: 1px solid lightgray]{18 \\pi}.\n\\]" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["a8942c70-e5be-58bd-9441-c89f4912e367"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "aba5c3d1-b904-56ff-b6f0-a46b86905b0d" :answer/id #uuid "aba5c3d1-b904-56ff-b6f0-a46b86905b0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x - 12 - \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dd23d842-a5d1-5918-948e-36db4983f82a" :answer/id #uuid "dd23d842-a5d1-5918-948e-36db4983f82a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x - 11 + \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "76c93819-5f94-5f71-9207-90527902ad17" :answer/id #uuid "76c93819-5f94-5f71-9207-90527902ad17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-11" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1117cafb-bea7-5676-bd0f-63daf7595db3" :answer/id #uuid "1117cafb-bea7-5676-bd0f-63daf7595db3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=- 11 x + 11 \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fa02d377-8768-52fe-b201-deaea37828d7" :answer/id #uuid "fa02d377-8768-52fe-b201-deaea37828d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9c494561-b4d8-5b70-a243-062936e00deb" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c494561-b4d8-5b70-a243-062936e00deb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["aba5c3d1-b904-56ff-b6f0-a46b86905b0d" "dd23d842-a5